## `_resolveProviderConfig` (session-manager.ts:1802–1832) — Azure handling

```ts
private _resolveProviderConfig(model?: string): Record<string, any> {
    const registry = this.workerDefaults.modelProviders;
    if (registry) {
        const resolved = registry.resolve(model);
        if (resolved) {
            if (resolved.type === "github") return {};
            if (resolved.sdkProvider) return { provider: resolved.sdkProvider };
        }
    }
    const p = this.workerDefaults.provider;
    if (!p) return {};
    if (p.type === "azure" && model && !p.baseUrl.includes("/deployments/")) {
        return { provider: { ...p, baseUrl: `${p.baseUrl.replace(/\/+$/, "")}/deployments/${model}` } };
    }
    return { provider: p };
}
```

**Registry path (lines 1803–1816):** Delegates to `ModelProviderRegistry.resolve(model)`, which normalizes `model` (`provider:model` or bare name), looks up the matching config, and detects Azure via `provider.type === "azure"`. If matched and `baseUrl` lacks `/deployments/`, it appends the **resolved canonical model name** (`desc.modelName`) as the deployment segment, defaults `apiVersion` to `"2024-10-21"` if unset, and resolves `apiKey` supporting `env:VAR_NAME` indirection. Returns `{ provider: resolved.sdkProvider }` as-is (GitHub type returns `{}` instead).

**Legacy path (lines 1818–1831):** Only runs if the registry is absent or resolves nothing. Uses the single deprecated `workerDefaults.provider` object, detecting Azure the same way (`p.type === "azure"`). Rewrites `baseUrl` similarly, but appends the **raw `model` argument** (not a resolved name), requires `model` to be truthy for the rewrite to fire, applies **no default `apiVersion`** (passes `p.azure` through unchanged), and does **no `env:` indirection** on `apiKey`.

**Key differences:** registry path uses resolved canonical model name + apiVersion default + env-key indirection + supports multiple providers via `model_providers.json`; legacy path uses the raw model string, no defaults/indirection, and assumes a single static provider config.
